{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"model":1,"htmlContent":7},{"name":2,"description":3,"url":4,"category":5,"subcategory":6},"Claude 3 Sonnet","Mid-tier of the original Claude 3 family. Retired 2025-07-21.","https://ai-tldr.dev/models/claude-3-sonnet/","Anthropic","Claude Sonnet","\u003Csection id=\"overview\" class=\"lrn-section\" aria-labelledby=\"overview-h\">\u003Ch2 class=\"lrn-h2\" id=\"overview-h\">\u003Cspan class=\"lrn-h2-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//\u003C/span> Overview\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"lrn-p\">Claude 3 Sonnet is the original Sonnet model, announced on March 4, 2024 as the balanced middle tier of the Claude 3 family, between Claude 3 Opus and Claude 3 Haiku. It introduced the Opus/Sonnet/Haiku naming that every later Claude generation has used.\u003C/p>\u003Cp class=\"lrn-p\">It was the first Claude model with vision, able to process photos, charts, graphs and technical diagrams alongside text. On standard benchmarks it scored 79.0% on MMLU, 40.4% on GPQA, 73.0% on HumanEval, and 92.3% on GSM8K, positioning it as a strong, affordable model for scaled enterprise deployments.\u003C/p>\u003Cp class=\"lrn-p\">Claude 3 Sonnet has a 200K token context window, up to 4,096 output tokens, an August 2023 knowledge cutoff, and supports text and image input, at $3 / $15 per million tokens. Its model ID is claude-3-sonnet-20240229; the snapshot was retired on July 21, 2025.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"lrn-table-wrap\">\u003Ctable class=\"lrn-table\">\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Released\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>2024-03-04\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">License\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Weights\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>API only\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Context\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>200K\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Max output\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>4K\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Architecture\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>Proprietary transformer (non-reasoning); first model in the Claude 3 family's middle tier.\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Knowledge cutoff\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>August 2023\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Modalities\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>Text, Vision\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Status\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>Deprecated\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003C/div>\u003C/section>\u003Csection id=\"benchmarks\" class=\"lrn-section\" aria-labelledby=\"benchmarks-h\">\u003Ch2 class=\"lrn-h2\" id=\"benchmarks-h\">\u003Cspan class=\"lrn-h2-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//\u003C/span> Benchmarks\u003C/h2>\u003Col class=\"mdl-chart\" aria-label=\"Benchmark scores\">\u003Cli class=\"mdl-chart-row\">\u003Ca class=\"mdl-chart-name\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-family\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" title=\"Source: anthropic.com\">MMLU\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-track\">\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-fill\" style=\"width:79%\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-val\">79%\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003Cli class=\"mdl-chart-row\">\u003Ca class=\"mdl-chart-name\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-family\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" title=\"Source: anthropic.com\">GPQA\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-track\">\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-fill\" style=\"width:40.4%\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-val\">40.4%\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003Cli class=\"mdl-chart-row\">\u003Ca class=\"mdl-chart-name\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-family\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" title=\"Source: anthropic.com\">HumanEval\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-track\">\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-fill\" style=\"width:73%\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-val\">73%\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003Cli class=\"mdl-chart-row\">\u003Ca class=\"mdl-chart-name\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-family\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" title=\"Source: anthropic.com\">GSM8K\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-track\">\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-fill\" style=\"width:92.3%\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-chart-val\">92.3%\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ol>\u003Cp class=\"mdl-chart-cap\">Scores on a 0–100 scale (25-point gridlines); higher is better. Each benchmark links to its published source.\u003C/p>\u003C/section>\u003Csection id=\"pricing\" class=\"lrn-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pricing-h\">\u003Ch2 class=\"lrn-h2\" id=\"pricing-h\">\u003Cspan class=\"lrn-h2-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//\u003C/span> Pricing\u003C/h2>\u003Cdiv class=\"lrn-table-wrap\">\u003Ctable class=\"lrn-table\">\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Input\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-price-amt\">$3.00\u003C/span> \u003Cspan class=\"mdl-price-unit\">per million tokens\u003C/span>\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth scope=\"row\">Output\u003C/th>\u003Ctd>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-price-amt\">$15.00\u003C/span> \u003Cspan class=\"mdl-price-unit\">per million tokens\u003C/span>\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"lrn-p\">\u003Ca href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-family\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Pricing source ↗\u003C/a>\u003C/p>\u003C/section>\u003Csection id=\"strengths\" class=\"lrn-section\" aria-labelledby=\"strengths-h\">\u003Ch2 class=\"lrn-h2\" id=\"strengths-h\">\u003Cspan class=\"lrn-h2-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//\u003C/span> Strengths\u003C/h2>\u003Cul class=\"lrn-list\">\u003Cli>Introduced the Opus/Sonnet/Haiku tier naming for the Claude family\u003C/li>\u003Cli>First Claude model with vision (charts, diagrams, photos)\u003C/li>\u003Cli>200K token context window at an affordable mid-tier price\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Balanced intelligence and speed for enterprise scale\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Solid math and coding scores (92.3% GSM8K, 73.0% HumanEval)\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/section>\u003Csection id=\"use-cases\" class=\"lrn-section\" aria-labelledby=\"use-cases-h\">\u003Ch2 class=\"lrn-h2\" id=\"use-cases-h\">\u003Cspan class=\"lrn-h2-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//\u003C/span> Best for\u003C/h2>\u003Cul class=\"lrn-list\">\u003Cli>General-purpose text generation and summarization\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Vision tasks over charts, graphs and technical diagrams\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Knowledge-base Q&amp;A and enterprise content workflows\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Cost-sensitive deployments needing a balanced model\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Math and coding assistance at moderate difficulty\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/section>\u003Csection id=\"access\" class=\"lrn-section\" aria-labelledby=\"access-h\">\u003Ch2 class=\"lrn-h2\" id=\"access-h\">\u003Cspan class=\"lrn-h2-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//\u003C/span> How to access\u003C/h2>\u003Cdiv class=\"lrn-table-wrap\">\u003Ctable class=\"lrn-table\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Provider\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Model ID\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-family\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Anthropic ↗\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>claude-3-sonnet-20240229\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/claude-in-amazon-bedrock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Amazon Bedrock ↗\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>anthropic.claude-3-sonnet-20240229-v1:0\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003C/div>\u003C/section>\u003Csection id=\"history\" class=\"lrn-section\" aria-labelledby=\"history-h\">\u003Ch2 class=\"lrn-h2\" id=\"history-h\">\u003Cspan class=\"lrn-h2-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//\u003C/span> Claude Sonnet — every version\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"lrn-p\">The full lineage of the Claude Sonnet line, newest first. Every version has its own page — click any to compare specs, benchmarks and pricing.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"lrn-table-wrap\">\u003Ctable class=\"lrn-table lrn-cmp\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Version\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Released\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Context\u003C/th>\u003Cth>License\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd class=\"lrn-cmp-name\">\u003Ca href=\"/models/claude-sonnet-5/\" data-internal=\"true\">Claude Sonnet 5\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"mdl-cmp-badge\">current\u003C/span>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2026-06-30\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>1M\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd class=\"lrn-cmp-name\">\u003Ca href=\"/models/claude-sonnet-4-6/\" data-internal=\"true\">Claude Sonnet 4.6\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2026-02-17\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>1M\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd class=\"lrn-cmp-name\">\u003Ca href=\"/models/claude-sonnet-4-5/\" data-internal=\"true\">Claude Sonnet 4.5\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2025-09-29\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>1M\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd class=\"lrn-cmp-name\">\u003Ca href=\"/models/claude-sonnet-4/\" data-internal=\"true\">Claude Sonnet 4\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2025-05-22\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>200K\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd class=\"lrn-cmp-name\">\u003Ca href=\"/models/claude-3-7-sonnet/\" data-internal=\"true\">Claude 3.7 Sonnet\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2025-02-24\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>200K\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd class=\"lrn-cmp-name\">\u003Ca href=\"/models/claude-3-5-sonnet-v2/\" data-internal=\"true\">Claude 3.5 Sonnet (new)\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2024-10-22\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>200K\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd class=\"lrn-cmp-name\">\u003Ca href=\"/models/claude-3-5-sonnet/\" data-internal=\"true\">Claude 3.5 Sonnet\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2024-06-20\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>200K\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr class=\"lrn-cmp-cur\">\u003Ctd class=\"lrn-cmp-name\">\u003Cstrong>Claude 3 Sonnet\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>2024-03-04\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>200K\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Proprietary\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003C/div>\u003C/section>\u003Csection id=\"faq\" class=\"lrn-section lrn-faq\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-h\">\u003Ch2 class=\"lrn-h2\" id=\"faq-h\">\u003Cspan class=\"lrn-h2-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//\u003C/span> FAQ\u003C/h2>\u003Cdetails class=\"lrn-faq-item\">\u003Csummary>When was Claude 3 Sonnet released?\u003C/summary>\u003Cp>It was announced on March 4, 2024 as the balanced middle tier of the Claude 3 family (Opus, Sonnet, Haiku).\u003C/p>\u003C/details>\u003Cdetails class=\"lrn-faq-item\">\u003Csummary>What were its benchmark scores?\u003C/summary>\u003Cp>79.0% on MMLU, 40.4% on GPQA, 73.0% on HumanEval, and 92.3% on GSM8K.\u003C/p>\u003C/details>\u003Cdetails class=\"lrn-faq-item\">\u003Csummary>What are its key specs?\u003C/summary>\u003Cp>200K token context window, up to 4,096 output tokens, an August 2023 knowledge cutoff, text and vision input, at $3/$15 per million tokens.\u003C/p>\u003C/details>\u003Cdetails class=\"lrn-faq-item\">\u003Csummary>Is Claude 3 Sonnet still available?\u003C/summary>\u003Cp>No. The claude-3-sonnet-20240229 snapshot was retired on July 21, 2025. Anthropic recommends Claude Sonnet 4.6 as the replacement.\u003C/p>\u003C/details>\u003C/section>"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
